,\"methods\":{\"constructor\":{\"params\":{\"initialOwner\":\"Administrative owner; only used to wire the factory once.\",\"feePolicy_\":\"Shared protocol/creator split policy, the same singleton the curve and hook read.\",\"feeEscrow_\":\"Shared claimable balance ledger releases are paid through.\\n     \"}},\"release(address)\":{\"details\":\"Restricted to the two parties a release pays. Letting anyone\\n     * choose when value leaves the vest is harmful in two ways. A caller can\\n     * time a release inside the protocol owner's creator-recipient recovery\\n     * window, flushing vested tokens to the very address the recovery exists\\n     * to abandon. A caller can also advance the checkpoint every second, so\\n     * each step rounds its newly vested amount down to zero and the vest\\n     * stalls without ever paying out.\\n     \"},\"vestingStart(address)\":{\"details\":\"Reporting only. Vesting is accounted from `vestedUnreleased`,\\n     * `unvestedAmount`, `lastUpdate` and `vestingEnd`, which are settled on\\n     * every lock and release. Interpolating this value against\\n     * `VESTING_DURATION` will not reproduce `vestedAmount`, because already\\n     * vested tokens are banked at each deposit rather than recomputed from\\n     * the shifted clock. Read `vestedAmount` for the authoritative figure.\\n     \"},\"pendingOwner()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the address of the pending owner.\\n     \"},\"transferOwnership(address)\":{\"details\":\"Starts the ownership transfer of the contract to a new account. Replaces the pending transfer if there is one.\\n     * Can only be called by the current owner.\\n     *\\n     * Setting `newOwner` to the zero address is allowed; this can be used to cancel an initiated ownership transfer.\\n     \"},\"acceptOwnership()\":{\"details\":\"The new owner accepts the ownership transfer.\\n     \"},\"owner()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the address of the current owner.\\n     \"}},\"errors\":{\"ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall()\":[{\"details\":\"Unauthorized reentrant call.\\n     \"}],\"OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(address)\":[{\"details\":\"The caller account is not authorized to perform an operation.\\n     \"}],\"OwnableInvalidOwner(address)\":[{\"details\":\"The owner is not a valid owner account. (eg. `address(0)`)\\n     \"}]},\"title\":\"PonsV2BuybackVault\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"setFactory(address)\":{\"notice\":\"One-time wiring of the v2 factory, set after both are\\n     * deployed, used to authorize each launch's bonding curve as a locker.\\n     \"},\"renounceOwnership()\":{\"notice\":\"Permanently disabled. Ownership here exists only to perform the\\n     * one-time factory wiring, and renouncing before that wiring would strand\\n     * every future buyback lock.\\n     \"},\"lock(address,uint256,address,address,uint16)\":{\"notice\":\"Locks `amount` of `token` into its five-year vest, preserving\\n     * the supplied beneficiaries and split for the active vesting epoch.\\n     * Restricted to the two legitimate callers for `token`'s own buyback:\\n     * the shared meme hook, or `token`'s own bonding curve looked up live\\n     * from the factory.\\n     \"},\"release(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Releases every currently vested, not-yet-released token for\\n     * `token`, using the beneficiaries and split frozen for its active\\n     * vesting epoch.\"},\"updateCreatorRecipient(address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Redirects a launch's buyback vest to a new creator recipient.\\n     * Restricted to the factory, which forwards both self-service creator\\n     * transfers and protocol-owner recovery overrides here, so vested\\n     * buyback tokens track the same recipient as immediate creator fees\\n     * rather than remaining stranded on the launch-time address. Vested but\\n     * not-yet-released tokens follow the new recipient too, matching the\\n     * intent of wallet recovery. Only the protocol split terms stay bound to\\n     * the launch snapshot; the creator identity is managed here instead.\\n     \"},\"totalLocked(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Total amount of `token` ever locked into this vault.\\n     \"},\"totalReleased(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Total amount of `token` already released from this vault.\\n     \"},\"vestingStart(address)\":{\"notice\":\"The launch's current weighted-average vesting start time.\"},\"vestedAmount(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Amount of `token` vested so far, released or not.\\n     \"},\"releasable(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Amount of `token` currently releasable: vested but not yet released.\\n     \"},\"vestingTerms(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the immutable terms for the token's active vesting epoch.\\n     \"}},\"notice\":\"Holds every launch's bought-back memecoin supply and releases it\\n * linearly over five years instead of burning it immediately, splitting\\n * every release between the creator and the protocol on the launch's\\n * recorded fee shares. One shared deployment serves every launch, the same\\n * \\\"single deployment for every token\\\" pattern PonsV2FeeEscrow already uses.\\n *\\n * Note that the split applies to the release, not to the funding. Both the\\n * curve and the hook carve the buyback slice out of the creator's share of\\n * the fees alone, so the creator funds the entire lock and then receives\\n * only their fee share of it back. Enabling a buyback therefore moves value\\n * from the creator to the protocol relative to taking the fees directly,\\n * by an amount that grows with `buybackBurnBps`.\\n *\\n * Deposits use a weighted-average vesting clock instead of per-deposit\\n * tranches: a launch's fee sweep can add to its lock on every single sweep,\\n * and tracking an unbounded array of tranches would make `release()`'s gas\\n * cost grow forever. Instead, each new deposit shifts the launch's single\\n * `vestingStart` forward by an amount proportional to the deposit's share\\n * of the new total, so a large existing lock is barely disturbed by a small\\n * top-up, and a small existing lock is pulled close to the new deposit's own\\n * clock. `vestedAmount` at any time reflects a fair, size-weighted blend\\n * across every deposit made so far.\\n \",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"lib/crane/contracts/protocols/launchpads/ponsFamily/v2/PonsV2BuybackVault.sol\":\"PonsV2BuybackVault\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/test/mocks/\",\"battlechain-lib/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/src/\",\"battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/\",\"chainlink-ccip/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/vendor/optimism/interop-lib/v0/src/\",\"chainlink-evm/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-evm/\",\"chainlink-local/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/src/\",\"clones/=lib/crane/contracts/external/clones-with-immutable-args/\",\"contracts/external/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/=lib/crane/contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/\",\"contracts/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"crane/=lib/crane/\",\"createx/=lib/crane/lib/bat